# AGENTS.md - <CATALOG_NAME>

This repository is a vignette catalog for one dataset.
`catalog.toml` is the routing manifest; notebooks are self-contained marimo programs and expose reusable top-level `@app.function` helpers.

## Restore project skills after clone

The installer-owned skill directories are gitignored.
Run these exact commands from the repository root:

```bash
npx skills@1.5.20 add carpenter-singh-lab/vignette-catalog-skills -s vignette-catalog-compose-notebook -s vignette-catalog-scaffold -a claude-code -a codex -y
npx skills@1.5.20 add marimo-team/marimo-pair -s marimo-pair -a claude-code -a codex -y
```

## Notebook work

Read `catalog.toml` and use `vignette-catalog-compose-notebook` before running or changing a notebook.
Open PEP 723 notebooks with `--sandbox`.
Reuse existing helpers instead of creating a parallel data-access path.
Inspect live outputs, then run the skill's `scripts/validate-notebook.sh` on every changed notebook.

## Dataset contract

- Surface: `<DATA_SURFACE>`.
- Record dataset-specific versions, auth, caches, hashes, identifiers, and caveats in this repository.
- Raw inputs are immutable; follow the existing data-directory policy for generated outputs.

